  "name": "Example: Computing the Greatest Common Divisor of Two Three-Digit Numbers",
  "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $713$ and $322.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}713 & = & 322(2) & + & 69 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 322 & = & 69(4) & + & 46 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 69 & = & 46(1) & + & 23 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 46 & = & 23(2) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is ${\\color{red}23}.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $713$ and $322$ is $23.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\textrm{gcd}(713, 322) = 23.\n$$",
